	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Thermal Energy} is the portion of the thermodynamic or internal energy of a system that is responsible for the temperature of the system. From a macroscopic thermodynamic description, the thermal energy of a system is given by its constant volume specific heat capacity C(T), a temperature coefficient also called thermal capacity, at any given absolute temperature (T): (U_{thermal = C(T) \\cdot T)."@en ;
